nce early September put her between nine and twelve points ahead of Republican Bobby Charles, including a Suffolk University survey in mid-October showing a 49-38 lead. Ratings from seven national outlets split between Solid D and Likely D, and prediction markets price her chances near 95 percent.\n\nPingree has also out-raised Charles roughly two to one, though independent Rick Bennett remains on the ballot after raising about $665,000 and could draw votes from both major parties. Maine's four-point Democratic lean gives the party a structural edge, and the campaign has been described as quiet, with four debates producing no clear turning point. Charles needs a substantial late shift to close a double-digit gap in a state where the fundamentals favor Democrats.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9757, "margin": 10.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9716, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9705, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9649, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.96, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9621, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.961, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9719, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9653, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9728, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9678, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9699, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9727, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.971, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.977, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9808, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9762, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9806, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9811, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13"